    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0651" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12566: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-12T18:00:00+08:00">December 12 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >16?</hi>], 1933—6 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>913. Department’s 394, December 16 [<hi rendition="#italic">14</hi>] 4 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">6</hi>] p.m. I have instructed Peck at Nanking to hand
                    to the Foreign Office an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> acknowledging
                    receipt of the Foreign Office note of November 25th and stating the position of
                    the American Government in the same terms as stated in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> handed by me to the Foreign Office on
                    May 19, 1930 which [was reported?] in the Legation’s telegram No. 355, May 21, 4
                    p.m., 1930.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d574-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
